WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:02.168 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I'm not just talking
about the left and liberals.

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.103
Let's not forget,

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:04.337
let's not have a short memory.

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:06.006 align:start size:81% position:19%
You know, when
this pandemic hit,

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:08.808
you actually tried to make me

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:10.343
work out things with Sam Harris.

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:11.544
I mean, we had conservatives,

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:12.746
people that were
more in the middle,

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:14.247
that were saying
"No, lockdowns now.

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:15.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
At least for now, at least
for a couple of weeks."

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:18.151 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I was always like,
"Hell no, hell no.

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:19.185
I know what this is,

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:20.520
it's paralyzing fear.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.554
You're showing us..."

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:23.089
Uniquely, even the death count.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:25.358
I mean, how bizarre for a
news organization to say,

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:26.526
"Stay at home,"

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:27.861 align:start size:84% position:16%
and then every
time somebody dies,

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:29.362
just add a number on the screen.

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:31.364
I mean, that's literally a
game of psychological fear,

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:32.799
right?

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:34.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I knew what was
coming around the corner.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:37.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it shocked me how much
people, left and right,

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:39.272 align:start size:84% position:16%
were willing to give
up their freedom

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:40.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they had a little
bit of fear, right?

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:41.641
It shocked me.

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:42.909
I wasn't one of them.

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:44.577
And I know that lot of
people have come around,

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:45.445
on the conservative side,

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:46.713
and said, "No more."

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:49.115
But, how do we get
people to understand

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:50.984 align:start size:97% position:3%
that we can't get to the point
where you say, "No more."

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:51.851
It has to be "Never,"

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:52.819
right in the beginning,

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:54.320
when you're feeling fearful.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.221 align:start size:97% position:3%
You can't say, "Well, I
was okay with the lockdowns

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:56.723
for two weeks.

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.091 align:start size:97% position:3%
But, you know what? One year's
a little too long for me."

00:00:58.091 --> 00:00:58.925
Right? You've already lost the-

00:00:58.925 --> 00:01:01.628
(intriguing music)

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:07.200 line:0%
- All right.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.468 line:0%
We are on location,

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:11.171 line:0%
on the set of Candice.

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:13.106 line:0%
And I'm with Candace Owens,

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:14.808
on your set, lady.

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:17.110 align:start size:88% position:13%
Not too shabby!
- I've come a long way.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.545
- You have come a long way.

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:20.580 align:start size:97% position:3%
- You've being one of my
first interviews on your set,

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.748
so there we go.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:22.982
- That's right.

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:24.350
Everyone knows the
story between us

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:25.218
and knows our history.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:26.052
But, real quick,

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:27.353
to recap in one minute,

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:30.056 align:start size:88% position:13%
when I brought you onto
my show originally,

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:31.524
we were doing YouTube Week.

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:34.961 align:start size:97% position:3%
We were just trying to
find like anyone on YouTube

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:36.196
doing anything interesting.

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:37.063
We found this girl,

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:38.498
Red Pill Black.

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:40.633
I did not know your name

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:42.268
until we sat down
in those chairs,

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:44.003
a minute before we started.

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:45.305
And now,

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:46.606
you've basically like
lit the world on fire.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:47.807
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:48.775 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's crazy to
think back at like,

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:50.176 line:0%
so much I didn't even know then.

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:51.544 line:0%
Like, I, obviously,

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:53.379 line:0%
was not looking to
get into politics.

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:55.014 line:0%
And if I look back
on that interview,

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:57.016
I feel so young, you know?

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:58.284
Like so,

00:01:58.284 --> 00:01:59.652
not really knowing what
I was stumbling upon,

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:00.854
but knowing I kinda
had this feeling

00:02:00.854 --> 00:02:01.921
that something was really wrong

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.890
and I had been lied to.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:04.891
And wow,

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:05.825
what a whirlwind it's been

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:07.260
over the last four years.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:08.728 align:start size:97% position:3%
- So, out of all the people
that I've interviewed,

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:10.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we've talked about
this many times privately.

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:13.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, out of all the
people that I interviewed,

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:14.734
we finished that
first interview,

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.269
I turned to David,

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:18.605
I was like, "That girl is
going to be a superstar."

00:02:18.605 --> 00:02:19.873
It was just so obvious.

00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:21.774
But, did you have
this plan at all?

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.243
Like, I know you
were kinda curious,

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:24.310
and you were figuring it out,

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:25.378
and there were one or two things

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:26.579
that I asked you about politics

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:27.981 align:start size:88% position:13%
that you were kinda
like, "I don't know yet.

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:29.616 align:start size:84% position:16%
I don't want to
comment on that yet."

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:31.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which I thought was pretty
impressive, actually.

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:34.053
But, you have just
like marched forward.

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:35.722 align:start size:84% position:16%
The machine has
tried to destroy you

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:36.623
how many times now?

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:37.857
- Yeah. (laughs)

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:38.892
- You keep a running count?

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:39.993
- Definitely have lost count.

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:42.228
And you know, I think, again,

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:44.397 align:start size:97% position:3%
kind of hinting at the naivety
of that first interview,

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:45.732 align:start size:84% position:16%
which is really
beautiful to watch,

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:47.367
is that I just never
could have imagined

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:48.635
that people would
try to destroy me.

00:02:48.635 --> 00:02:50.136 align:start size:81% position:19%
I never would have
imagined, even,

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:52.739
that I wasn't allowed to not
have an opinion on some things,

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:54.607
that I wasn't allowed
to grow as a person

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:55.575
and say, "I'm still learning."

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:57.410
Because I was still learning.

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:59.512 align:start size:84% position:16%
I had ideas and
feelings about things,

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:01.581 align:start size:88% position:13%
but I didn't really have
the facts on my side.

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:04.250
And I had no idea that
when you're in politics,

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:05.685 align:start size:84% position:16%
they're just looking
to expose you.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:07.153 align:start size:81% position:19%
And "She's a fake,
she's a fraud.

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:08.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, look, she doesn't
know this, she's stupid."

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:10.657
So, I had to grow up
pretty quick, you know?

00:03:10.657 --> 00:03:14.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
And really kind of sharpen
my figurative sword,

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.094
and really get ready,

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:16.796
and do a lot of studying.

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:17.730
But, yeah,

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.165
I could have never imagined.

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:20.967 align:start position:0%
I had no plan. I was just
saying what I thought to be real

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:22.569
and what I thought to be true.

00:03:22.569 --> 00:03:24.437
- Yeah. And I know that
you're not just saying it

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:25.905
because every time
I've been with you,

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:28.208
when we've done road gigs
together, or whatever,

00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:29.475
you've got ten books with you.

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:31.010 align:start size:84% position:16%
We had dinner at your
house last night,

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:32.445
you're working on farming now.

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:35.582 align:start size:97% position:3%
Like, you're always just
trying to learn more and more.

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:38.017 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I will be welcomed at
your off-location site, right?

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:39.219
When the grid goes down

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:40.153 align:start size:97% position:3%
and everything else happens.
- Yeah,

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:40.820
when the grid goes down, yeah.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.355
I, actually,

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:43.523
as you just hinted on,

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:44.757 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm kinda going
through this thing now

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:47.894
where I realize that
we are all dependents,

00:03:47.894 --> 00:03:49.495
and we are all on welfare,

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:51.397
if we don't know how to grow
food and support ourselves.

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:53.066
And I think that
that really speaks

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:55.868 align:start size:84% position:16%
to the drama of
this administration,

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.337
of realizing that...

00:03:57.337 --> 00:03:58.404
I know a lot of Americans

00:03:58.404 --> 00:03:59.973
empathize with the idea

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:01.407 align:start size:88% position:13%
that we feel like we're
losing our country,

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:03.943 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
and that we really have
communists in the White House.

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.511 line:0%
And you know,

00:04:05.511 --> 00:04:07.614 line:0%
we are watching all of
Americans be depressed.

00:04:07.614 --> 00:04:09.082
And, in that vein,

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:10.316
I said to myself,

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:11.784
"If this really
does hit," right?

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:13.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
"If we are suddenly living
in a communist country

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:14.153
in three years, four years,

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:15.788
or however you wanna call it,

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:17.490
can I fend for myself?"
- Two months, I think.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.058
- Yeah, two months, right.

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:20.927
"Can I fend for myself?
Can I grow my own food?

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:22.929 align:start size:88% position:13%
What do I know about
living off of the land?"

00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:24.163
So, that is something,

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:25.698
yeah, that I'm just
now learning now.

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:27.867
And what better place to do
it than in Tennessee, right?

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:31.070
I mean, everybody's
farming, hunting.

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:32.538
So, yeah,

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:33.806 align:start size:97% position:3%
that's kind of another thing
that I'm exploring now.

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:35.041
- Can you believe that
you live in Tennessee?

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:36.643 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, I said to
you guys last night,

00:04:36.643 --> 00:04:38.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
like you so were obviously
in the right place.

00:04:38.378 --> 00:04:39.212
So happy,

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:40.146
and the house is great,

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:41.080
and little George is great.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:42.615
Like, you've just embraced it.

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:43.850
But, do you kind of sit back

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:45.285 align:start size:84% position:16%
and go, "Wow, I ended
up in Tennessee.

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:46.619
Five years ago,

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:48.588
little YouTuber from Philly,

00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:49.489
and here I am now."

00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:50.923
And on your own set,

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:51.891
with your own crew,

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:53.026
and the whole thing.

00:04:53.026 --> 00:04:54.527 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Married to an
Englishman in Tennessee.

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:56.663
If you had said to me that
first day that we sat down,

00:04:56.663 --> 00:04:58.164 align:start size:84% position:16%
like, "Here's
what's gonna happen.

00:04:58.164 --> 00:05:00.500
You're gonna end up living
in Nashville, Tennessee,

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.768 align:start size:88% position:13%
and you're gonna be
married to an Englishman

00:05:01.768 --> 00:05:03.036
that you will have
gotten engaged to

00:05:03.036 --> 00:05:05.805
after two weeks of
knowing each other."

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:07.040 align:start size:84% position:16%
I would have thought
you were nuts.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.641
And my life has
been pretty nuts,

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:10.576
and pretty unpredictable.

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:12.178
Tennessee, in my heart,

00:05:12.178 --> 00:05:13.980
I think I maybe thought
I would end up in Texas.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:14.814
I love Texas,

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:15.948
I love the Texans.

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:17.116
And, obviously,

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:18.751 align:start size:84% position:16%
opportunity came
knocking in Tennessee.

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:20.019
And now that I'm here,

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:21.621
I could never imagine
living anywhere else.

00:05:21.621 --> 00:05:23.489
Like, this is fully where
we wanna raise our family.

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:25.124 align:start size:81% position:19%
We think it is the
greatest state.

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:26.592
We love the people.

00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:28.127
There really is something
about the Tennesseans.

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:29.062
- Yeah.

00:05:29.062 --> 00:05:30.029
Do you think America is just,

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:31.297
this is how it's gonna be,

00:05:31.297 --> 00:05:33.433 align:start size:84% position:16%
you're just gonna
have to move to places

00:05:33.433 --> 00:05:34.934 align:start size:84% position:16%
that are more in line
with your values?

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:37.537
Or, is there a point
of someone staying

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:39.806
in say, California, or New York,

00:05:39.806 --> 00:05:40.740
and fighting?

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:41.741
Do you think that that point,

00:05:41.741 --> 00:05:43.176
have we crossed that already?

00:05:43.176 --> 00:05:44.644
- I do not think

00:05:44.644 --> 00:05:46.145 align:start size:97% position:3%
that there will ever be a
clean election in California.

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:47.413
I think that Gavin Newsom

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:49.315
has made sure that
that can't happen.

00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:50.550
To say,

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:52.352
"mail-in ballots
into perpetuity"?

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:53.753
Forget it, no.

00:05:53.753 --> 00:05:54.987
New York City,

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:56.756
I don't have much
hope for either.

00:05:56.756 --> 00:05:58.024
I can't imagine...

00:05:58.024 --> 00:05:59.559
I mean, when I go
to New York City,

00:05:59.559 --> 00:06:01.361
it's like already stepping
into a communist country,

00:06:01.361 --> 00:06:04.063
where the people are okay
with their oppressions.

00:06:04.063 --> 00:06:06.232
I mean, the idea of
having to show papers

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:08.167
every time you walk
into a restaurant,

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:09.936
or have a transaction,

00:06:09.936 --> 00:06:11.304
that's actually not America.

00:06:11.304 --> 00:06:12.572
So, I would almost say

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:13.740
that that's not a
future prediction,

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:14.674
that's a present one,

00:06:14.674 --> 00:06:16.209
like in New York and California.

00:06:16.209 --> 00:06:17.977
And I should say
more Los Angeles,

00:06:17.977 --> 00:06:19.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
I shouldn't say the whole
state of California.

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:23.316
But, those are not
American cities.

00:06:23.316 --> 00:06:24.951
- What has that told you about,

00:06:24.951 --> 00:06:27.086 align:start size:88% position:13%
or what have you learned
about just humans?

00:06:27.086 --> 00:06:29.522
The way a certain set of
people just want more.

00:06:29.522 --> 00:06:31.090
That's what I feel
like in Los Angeles,

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:32.325
when I walk around.

00:06:32.325 --> 00:06:34.727 align:start size:81% position:19%
I'm like, "Man,
you guys like this

00:06:34.727 --> 00:06:36.629
and you're begging
for more control."

00:06:36.629 --> 00:06:39.699
That's been a very weird
thing to kinda realize.

00:06:39.699 --> 00:06:40.500
- Yeah.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:41.901
What it says to me

00:06:41.901 --> 00:06:44.704
is that fear is one
hell of a currency.

00:06:44.704 --> 00:06:46.806
And I have been hitting
on this on my own show,

00:06:46.806 --> 00:06:49.008
of making people
aware of the fact

00:06:49.008 --> 00:06:50.476 align:start size:84% position:16%
that the second
somebody can identify

00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:52.245
what it is that you
are fearful over,

00:06:52.245 --> 00:06:53.980
they can exert control over you.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:57.283
And I don't think that we have
ever seen that displayed more

00:06:57.283 --> 00:06:59.085 align:start size:84% position:16%
than in the COVID-19
circumstances.

00:06:59.085 --> 00:07:00.753 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I'm not just talking
about the left and liberals.

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:01.687
Let's not forget,

00:07:01.687 --> 00:07:03.389
let's not have a short memory.

00:07:03.389 --> 00:07:05.057 align:start size:81% position:19%
You know, when
this pandemic hit,

00:07:05.057 --> 00:07:07.860
you actually tried to make me

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.395
work out things with Sam Harris.

00:07:09.395 --> 00:07:10.596
I mean, we had conservatives,

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:11.798
people that were
more in the middle,

00:07:11.798 --> 00:07:13.299
that were saying
"No, lockdowns now.

00:07:13.299 --> 00:07:14.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
At least for now, at least
for a couple of weeks."

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:17.203 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I was always like,
"Hell no, hell no.

00:07:17.203 --> 00:07:18.171
I know what this is,

00:07:18.171 --> 00:07:19.572
it's paralyzing fear.

00:07:19.572 --> 00:07:20.573
You're showing us..."

00:07:20.573 --> 00:07:22.141
Uniquely, even the death count.

00:07:22.141 --> 00:07:23.409
I mean, how bizarre

00:07:23.409 --> 00:07:24.944
for a news organization
to say, "Stay at home."

00:07:24.944 --> 00:07:26.879 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then, every
time somebody dies,

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:28.181
just add a number on the screen.

00:07:28.181 --> 00:07:29.415
I mean,

00:07:29.415 --> 00:07:30.383
that's literally a game
of psychological fear,

00:07:30.383 --> 00:07:31.818
right?

00:07:31.818 --> 00:07:33.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I knew what was
coming around the corner.

00:07:33.586 --> 00:07:36.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it shocked me how much
people, left and right,

00:07:36.689 --> 00:07:38.291 align:start size:84% position:16%
were willing to give
up their freedom

00:07:38.291 --> 00:07:39.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they had a little
bit of fear, right?

00:07:39.725 --> 00:07:40.660
It shocked me.

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:41.894
I wasn't one of them.

00:07:41.894 --> 00:07:43.563
And I know that lot of
people have come around,

00:07:43.563 --> 00:07:44.430
on the conservative side,

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:45.665
and said "No more."

00:07:45.665 --> 00:07:48.100
But, how do we get
people to understand

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:50.002 align:start size:97% position:3%
that we can't get to the
point where you say "No more."

00:07:50.002 --> 00:07:50.837
It has to be, "Never,"

00:07:50.837 --> 00:07:51.771
right in the beginning,

00:07:51.771 --> 00:07:53.239
when you're feeling fearful.

00:07:53.239 --> 00:07:54.207 align:start size:97% position:3%
You can't say, "Well, I
was okay with the lockdowns

00:07:54.207 --> 00:07:55.041
for two weeks.

00:07:55.041 --> 00:07:56.242
But, you know what?

00:07:56.242 --> 00:07:57.610 align:start size:88% position:13%
One year is a little
too long for me." Right?

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:59.078
You've already lost the game.

00:07:59.078 --> 00:08:00.446 align:start position:0%
- Right, as we're about to roll
into year three, basically.

00:08:00.446 --> 00:08:01.247
- Right.

00:08:01.247 --> 00:08:02.081
It was never okay.

00:08:02.081 --> 00:08:02.915
- Yeah.

00:08:02.915 --> 00:08:04.116
- And I think that,

00:08:04.116 --> 00:08:06.018 align:start size:84% position:16%
because I'm a bit
more of a gut player,

00:08:06.018 --> 00:08:08.154 align:start size:84% position:16%
and because I
truly do understand

00:08:08.154 --> 00:08:10.089
how sinister governments can be,

00:08:10.089 --> 00:08:12.725 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's been the story of
human history since forever,

00:08:12.725 --> 00:08:14.861
I'm never willing to give
up a little bit of freedom

00:08:14.861 --> 00:08:17.763 align:start size:97% position:3%
for a little bit of safety.
- It's so funny to me

00:08:17.763 --> 00:08:19.966 align:start size:84% position:16%
because since I
know you privately,

00:08:19.966 --> 00:08:21.467
and as a friend,

00:08:21.467 --> 00:08:23.302
I know that the stuff that
you talk about publicly,

00:08:23.302 --> 00:08:24.537
even when I'm like, "Ah,

00:08:24.537 --> 00:08:26.038
Candace went a little
overboard on that one."

00:08:26.038 --> 00:08:26.873
I'm like,

00:08:26.873 --> 00:08:27.707
"I know that is you.

00:08:27.707 --> 00:08:28.641
That really is you."

00:08:28.641 --> 00:08:30.576
And we told this story once,

00:08:30.576 --> 00:08:32.445
but the day that
lockdown started,

00:08:32.445 --> 00:08:33.813
you were on my show in LA.

00:08:33.813 --> 00:08:35.815
We didn't know, at the
time we were taping,

00:08:35.815 --> 00:08:37.083
that lockdowns were
about to happen.

00:08:37.083 --> 00:08:37.950
- Right.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.218
- You were, literally,

00:08:39.218 --> 00:08:40.720
coughing up blood.

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:42.388
You were coughing up blood.

00:08:42.388 --> 00:08:43.990
Your friend, or your
assistant at the time,

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:45.191
was there also.

00:08:45.191 --> 00:08:46.592
She was sick.

00:08:46.592 --> 00:08:47.860
David's looking at me like,

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:49.161
"We're gonna be trapped
in the house for months

00:08:49.161 --> 00:08:50.096
with Candace.

00:08:50.096 --> 00:08:50.930
You could die here.

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:51.931
Like, it's all over."

00:08:51.931 --> 00:08:53.666
But, you were just like, "No,

00:08:53.666 --> 00:08:55.167
I don't have COVID, I'm fine.

00:08:55.167 --> 00:08:56.903
It has something to do with
the pillows at the hotel.

00:08:56.903 --> 00:08:58.404
And everyone's insane,

00:08:58.404 --> 00:08:59.472
and I'm gonna get the
hell out of here."

00:08:59.472 --> 00:09:00.640
- Yeah.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:01.807 align:start size:88% position:13%
That was so funny,
actually, in retrospect.

00:09:01.807 --> 00:09:03.242
Like, the worst timing

00:09:03.242 --> 00:09:04.744 align:start size:97% position:3%
of me having an allergic
reaction to feathered pillows.

00:09:04.744 --> 00:09:05.945
And like your husband
was not buying it.

00:09:05.945 --> 00:09:06.779
He's like, "No, no, no,

00:09:06.779 --> 00:09:08.014
she's dying of COVID."

00:09:08.014 --> 00:09:09.916
Like, Googling to see
what was happening.

00:09:09.916 --> 00:09:11.150
But, yeah.

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:12.752
And that was actually
the last event I did

00:09:12.752 --> 00:09:14.153 align:start size:88% position:13%
before they sort of
locked down everything,

00:09:14.153 --> 00:09:16.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
and all my events
necessarily got canceled.

00:09:16.856 --> 00:09:17.790
But, not because of me,

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:19.725
I mean, I attended everything.

00:09:19.725 --> 00:09:20.726
I was pregnant during COVID,

00:09:20.726 --> 00:09:21.761
I traveled the country,

00:09:21.761 --> 00:09:23.029
I traveled the world.

00:09:23.029 --> 00:09:24.297
I went to Croatia,

00:09:24.297 --> 00:09:25.231
I went to England.

00:09:25.231 --> 00:09:27.099
I just did not have this fear.

00:09:27.099 --> 00:09:28.568
I can't explain it.

00:09:28.568 --> 00:09:30.403
It was too convenient.

00:09:30.403 --> 00:09:31.571
And it also, obviously,

00:09:31.571 --> 00:09:33.139
didn't help their case

00:09:33.139 --> 00:09:35.408
that they had predicted
the coronavirus pandemic

00:09:35.408 --> 00:09:37.710
at The World Economic
Forum, a year prior.

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:39.445 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think what we're
dealing with right now

00:09:39.445 --> 00:09:43.015 align:start size:88% position:13%
is a very sinister,
evil, globalist agenda.

00:09:43.015 --> 00:09:44.083
And that is not a conspiracy,

00:09:44.083 --> 00:09:45.017
I think that is a fact.

00:09:45.017 --> 00:09:47.520
And they want to exert control

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:49.722 align:start size:84% position:16%
over every single
element of our lives.

00:09:49.722 --> 00:09:50.990
And, unfortunately,

00:09:50.990 --> 00:09:52.959
you have people that are
pliable to that control

00:09:52.959 --> 00:09:54.160
because they're fearful.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:55.828
And also, people
that are just lazy.

00:09:55.828 --> 00:09:57.029
So, one element

00:09:57.029 --> 00:09:58.497 align:start size:84% position:16%
is that people are
happy to be controlled

00:09:58.497 --> 00:09:59.699
because they're fearful.

00:09:59.699 --> 00:10:01.400 align:start size:88% position:13%
The other element is
because control is easy.

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:02.568
If you don't have to
think for yourself,

00:10:02.568 --> 00:10:04.136 align:start size:88% position:13%
and somebody just
plugs you into a system

00:10:04.136 --> 00:10:05.204
and says, "Do this."

00:10:05.204 --> 00:10:06.038
I mean,

00:10:06.038 --> 00:10:07.373
freedom is hard.

00:10:07.373 --> 00:10:08.307
Freedom is hard work.

00:10:08.307 --> 00:10:09.875
Personal responsibility is hard.

00:10:09.875 --> 00:10:10.910
Growing your own vegetables.

00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:12.411
Hey, that's pretty hard.

00:10:12.411 --> 00:10:13.479 align:start size:97% position:3%
Right? It's kinda easy to
just go to the grocery store

00:10:13.479 --> 00:10:14.480
and have it being prepared.

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:16.015
- Yeah.

00:10:16.015 --> 00:10:17.350
- People don't like to do
things that are difficult,

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:18.884
they want things to be
handed easily for them.

00:10:18.884 --> 00:10:20.553
And that's why we
have, you know,

00:10:20.553 --> 00:10:23.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
the extraordinary welfare
system that we have.

00:10:23.089 --> 00:10:24.790
- Why are you not afraid?

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:26.192
I know you're not.

00:10:26.192 --> 00:10:27.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, everyone is basically
afraid, seemingly.

00:10:27.827 --> 00:10:28.661
But, I dunno,

00:10:28.661 --> 00:10:29.895
is it your wiring?

00:10:29.895 --> 00:10:31.030 align:start size:84% position:16%
Is it something you
learned very early on?

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:32.898
Like, why do you always...

00:10:32.898 --> 00:10:34.300
You see the thing
in the distance

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:36.035
and you just go right to it.

00:10:36.035 --> 00:10:38.604 align:start size:97% position:3%
For as many times as Twitter
tried to take you out,

00:10:38.604 --> 00:10:40.506
or New York Times,
or whoever it is,

00:10:40.506 --> 00:10:42.475
you just keep going,
and going, and going.

00:10:42.475 --> 00:10:43.676
- Yeah.

00:10:43.676 --> 00:10:45.244 align:start size:84% position:16%
I get that question
all the time.

00:10:45.244 --> 00:10:48.514
And the truth is that I'm my
Granddaddy's Granddaughter.

00:10:48.514 --> 00:10:50.182
I mean, he just was a tough guy.

00:10:50.182 --> 00:10:51.417
He just passed in September.

00:10:51.417 --> 00:10:53.352 align:start size:84% position:16%
I've just dedicated
my book to him,

00:10:53.352 --> 00:10:54.186
my first book to him.

00:10:54.186 --> 00:10:55.488
And, you know,

00:10:55.488 --> 00:10:57.256
I have just always
looked at my life

00:10:57.256 --> 00:10:58.424
in comparison to his.

00:10:58.424 --> 00:11:00.026
And it's the reason why,

00:11:00.026 --> 00:11:01.527 align:start size:84% position:16%
when people talk about
their oppression,

00:11:01.527 --> 00:11:03.362
I think of a man who grew
up in segregated South,

00:11:03.362 --> 00:11:06.799 align:start size:97% position:3%
who never, ever, ever spoke
about being oppressed,

00:11:06.799 --> 00:11:08.768
never spoke about why
people were racist,

00:11:08.768 --> 00:11:11.070
never spoke about how the
white man was after him.

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:12.738
He just got up every
day and he worked.

00:11:12.738 --> 00:11:14.640
And he did that from the
time he was five-years-old

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:16.008
on a sharecropping farm.

00:11:16.008 --> 00:11:18.010 align:start size:84% position:16%
I find this generation
of individuals

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:19.512
to be a little bit pathetic.

00:11:19.512 --> 00:11:20.680
I think we're a little bit
pathetic. I think, you know,

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:23.382 align:start size:88% position:13%
the Greatest Generation
that ever lived,

00:11:23.382 --> 00:11:25.885 align:start size:97% position:3%
yielded the most pathetic
generation that's ever lived,

00:11:25.885 --> 00:11:27.620
which is walking among us today.

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:29.388 align:start size:88% position:13%
We just can't do
anything for ourselves.

00:11:29.388 --> 00:11:31.290
And I don't wanna be that.

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:33.693
And the other thing is
I'm just wired this way.

00:11:33.693 --> 00:11:35.695
I was like this since
I was a little girl.

00:11:35.695 --> 00:11:37.329 align:start size:84% position:16%
My parents always
tell stories about me.

00:11:37.329 --> 00:11:39.231
Like, I was just one of
those precocious kids

00:11:39.231 --> 00:11:41.701
that just never allowed an adult

00:11:41.701 --> 00:11:44.503
to tell me what to
do without reason.

00:11:44.503 --> 00:11:46.672
I never responded to
arbitrary authority.

00:11:46.672 --> 00:11:47.907
I was one of those kids that,

00:11:47.907 --> 00:11:49.041
if your parents were like,

00:11:49.041 --> 00:11:50.376
"Well, clean your bed

00:11:50.376 --> 00:11:51.677
or Santa's not gonna come."

00:11:51.677 --> 00:11:53.012
I would say like, "You
tell him not to come."

00:11:53.012 --> 00:11:53.846
Right?

00:11:53.846 --> 00:11:55.114
(David laughing)

00:11:55.114 --> 00:11:56.382
And so, they were
always laughing,

00:11:56.382 --> 00:11:57.917
and having to close a
door to reprimand me

00:11:57.917 --> 00:12:00.086
because I was kind of
like this little adult.

00:12:00.086 --> 00:12:03.355 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I think my
character is really just

00:12:03.355 --> 00:12:06.792
that I respect authority,

00:12:06.792 --> 00:12:08.394
but the authority
can't be arbitrary.

00:12:08.394 --> 00:12:09.395
It needs to make sense.

00:12:09.395 --> 00:12:11.330 line:0%
And if it doesn't make sense,

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:12.965 line:0%
and you're okay with it,

00:12:12.965 --> 00:12:15.134 line:0%
then that sets up the
grounds for slavery.

00:12:15.134 --> 00:12:16.802
And I'm not a slave.

00:12:16.802 --> 00:12:18.037
- You are not a slave,

00:12:18.037 --> 00:12:19.205
that is for sure.

00:12:19.205 --> 00:12:21.640
But, will you be a politician?

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:24.143 align:start position:0%
- Will I be a politician? I
get this question all the time.

00:12:24.143 --> 00:12:25.344
And I used to say "No,"

00:12:25.344 --> 00:12:28.414 align:start size:81% position:19%
and now I say,
"Never say never."

00:12:28.414 --> 00:12:30.049 align:start size:97% position:3%
I've had those conversations
with my husband before

00:12:30.049 --> 00:12:32.952 align:start size:84% position:16%
about what it would
actually mean.

00:12:32.952 --> 00:12:34.420
And I definitely would
never be in Congress,

00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:35.821
I can tell you, absolutely not.

00:12:35.821 --> 00:12:36.956
I've done two of those hearings.

00:12:36.956 --> 00:12:37.890
I would rather, honestly,

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:39.959
pull out all of my fingernails.

00:12:39.959 --> 00:12:41.427
- That was one of
your best moments.

00:12:41.427 --> 00:12:44.396
The one with you and Ted
Lieu was really incredible.

00:12:44.396 --> 00:12:45.231
And then, remember,

00:12:45.231 --> 00:12:46.665
we had that event.

00:12:46.665 --> 00:12:47.800 align:start position:0%
I forget, I don't even remember
where we were that night.

00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:49.168
But, you left that event,

00:12:49.168 --> 00:12:51.604
you destroyed everyone there,

00:12:51.604 --> 00:12:53.005
and then you just go
on with your life.

00:12:53.005 --> 00:12:53.839
- "Bye," yeah.

00:12:53.839 --> 00:12:55.040
I mean,

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:56.175 align:start size:84% position:16%
these people are
just are real losers,

00:12:56.175 --> 00:12:57.143
heading up all these hearings.

00:12:57.143 --> 00:12:58.410
But-

00:12:58.410 --> 00:12:59.678
- But, are you nervous
in any of those things?

00:12:59.678 --> 00:13:00.679
Like, I do this
for a living too,

00:13:00.679 --> 00:13:01.914
and I don't really get nervous,

00:13:01.914 --> 00:13:03.449 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I haven't sat
in front of Congress

00:13:03.449 --> 00:13:05.317
and just destroyed them.

00:13:05.317 --> 00:13:06.218
- Let me tell you something,

00:13:06.218 --> 00:13:07.153
Congress works for you,

00:13:07.153 --> 00:13:07.987
not the other way around.

00:13:07.987 --> 00:13:09.522
I actually think

00:13:09.522 --> 00:13:10.623
that the way that that whole
little auditorium is set up

00:13:10.623 --> 00:13:11.457
is wrong.

00:13:11.457 --> 00:13:12.291
Why are they above me?

00:13:12.291 --> 00:13:13.125
I should be-

00:13:13.125 --> 00:13:14.326
- Literally, they're...

00:13:14.326 --> 00:13:15.795 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah, they're
literally above you.

00:13:15.795 --> 00:13:17.029 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I believe that we should
literally be above them.

00:13:17.029 --> 00:13:18.364 align:start size:84% position:16%
I don't even like
the way it's set up.

00:13:18.364 --> 00:13:19.298
And this is the idea.

00:13:19.298 --> 00:13:20.199
We've gotten this idea

00:13:20.199 --> 00:13:21.367
that they're above us,

00:13:21.367 --> 00:13:22.301
they're not.

00:13:22.301 --> 00:13:23.235
They literally work for us.

00:13:23.235 --> 00:13:25.004
And the majority of them,

00:13:25.004 --> 00:13:26.906
on the Democrat side,

00:13:26.906 --> 00:13:28.174
are a bunch of scumbags.

00:13:28.174 --> 00:13:30.009
And they're working to
destroy this country.

00:13:30.009 --> 00:13:31.610
They've sold us out.

00:13:31.610 --> 00:13:33.479
A lot of them have
been in DC forever,

00:13:33.479 --> 00:13:35.314 align:start position:0%
and are just corrupt and trying
to fill their own pockets.

00:13:35.314 --> 00:13:36.515
So, I had no fear.

00:13:36.515 --> 00:13:38.584 align:start size:81% position:19%
I was angry at
the obvious set up

00:13:38.584 --> 00:13:40.586
and the attempt to play me.

00:13:40.586 --> 00:13:42.087
And I was happy

00:13:42.087 --> 00:13:43.756
that I was able to expose
them for what they were.

00:13:43.756 --> 00:13:46.125
But, I don't have fear of people

00:13:46.125 --> 00:13:48.260 align:start size:84% position:16%
that are essentially
my employees.

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:51.096 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Do you have anyone that
you've been trying to talk to,

00:13:51.096 --> 00:13:52.198
to get into a debate with,

00:13:52.198 --> 00:13:53.499
that has refused?

00:13:53.499 --> 00:13:54.767
There's gotta be some.

00:13:54.767 --> 00:13:56.669
But, you've done
a couple of these.

00:13:56.669 --> 00:13:57.970
Like, with Russell Brand,

00:13:57.970 --> 00:13:58.938
who you had major
differences with,

00:13:58.938 --> 00:13:59.972
and a couple other people.

00:13:59.972 --> 00:14:01.207
I find it very hard

00:14:01.207 --> 00:14:02.474
to get these people
to talk at this point

00:14:02.474 --> 00:14:04.944 align:start size:84% position:16%
because we are racist,
homophobic, bigots.

