the Candace that I know,

00:20:59.758 --> 00:21:01.593
not the Candace that
everybody else knows.

00:21:01.593 --> 00:21:02.427
- Yeah.

00:21:02.427 --> 00:21:03.262
I think, for me,

00:21:03.262 --> 00:21:05.831
the next few years,

00:21:05.831 --> 00:21:07.766
every day really is
about family for me.

00:21:07.766 --> 00:21:09.067 align:start size:88% position:13%
Like, I don't think
people really get to see

00:21:09.067 --> 00:21:10.269
the personal side of me

00:21:10.269 --> 00:21:11.536 align:start size:84% position:16%
because you can't
let them in politics.

00:21:11.536 --> 00:21:13.772
You know, (laughs)
they're just evil.

00:21:13.772 --> 00:21:15.507 align:start size:81% position:19%
But, I try to just
tell everybody

00:21:15.507 --> 00:21:17.075
that, "Family is the
most important thing,"

00:21:17.075 --> 00:21:18.176
every single day.

00:21:18.176 --> 00:21:19.344
And I try to,

00:21:19.344 --> 00:21:21.513 align:start size:88% position:13%
if I can prescribe
anything upon the world,

00:21:21.513 --> 00:21:23.115
it would be read the "Bible."

00:21:23.115 --> 00:21:24.349 align:start size:84% position:16%
Not because you need
to be religious,

00:21:24.349 --> 00:21:25.817
but because it has good values.

00:21:25.817 --> 00:21:26.652
You know what I mean?

00:21:26.652 --> 00:21:27.819
Read the "Bible"

00:21:27.819 --> 00:21:29.254 align:start size:88% position:13%
as you would read
"Aesop's Fables,' right?

00:21:29.254 --> 00:21:31.423 align:start size:97% position:3%
There's just good moralities
and lessons in there.

00:21:31.423 --> 00:21:32.924
And I definitely am someone

00:21:32.924 --> 00:21:34.826
that like, I'll just
peruse and read things.

00:21:34.826 --> 00:21:36.395 align:start size:81% position:19%
And you go through
the scriptures

00:21:36.395 --> 00:21:37.996
and you realize that...

00:21:37.996 --> 00:21:39.064
You walk away with
an understanding

00:21:39.064 --> 00:21:40.299
that evil is evil,

00:21:40.299 --> 00:21:42.200
and it can always get more evil,

00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:44.002
but in the end, goodness wins.

00:21:44.002 --> 00:21:46.338
And I think that we
have to understand

00:21:46.338 --> 00:21:47.906
that nothing is going to change

00:21:47.906 --> 00:21:50.676
until we take care of
our households first.

00:21:50.676 --> 00:21:52.177
Maybe this is the
Jordan Peterson,

00:21:52.177 --> 00:21:53.011
"Make your bed."

00:21:53.011 --> 00:21:54.079
Right?

00:21:54.079 --> 00:21:55.947
So, invest that time,

00:21:55.947 --> 00:21:57.516
when the world seems evil,

00:21:57.516 --> 00:22:00.419
invest that time in making
your home a better place,

00:22:00.419 --> 00:22:02.421 align:start size:88% position:13%
and making good personal
individual decisions.

00:22:02.421 --> 00:22:04.389 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I think that
enough of us do that

00:22:04.389 --> 00:22:07.392 align:start size:97% position:3%
and we save this place.
- I gotta tell you, Candace,

00:22:07.392 --> 00:22:09.628 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's weird 'cause we do
this publicly and privately,

00:22:09.628 --> 00:22:12.297 align:start size:84% position:16%
